# The Paperclip core commit CI checks Tickler against.
#
# Tickler's `@paperclipai/*` dev dependencies are `link:` references to a
# Paperclip checkout (CONTRIBUTING.md, "Never modify Paperclip core"). CI
# clones that checkout read-only from the public upstream so typecheck, build,
# and test can run against the real host types instead of stubs.
#
# Pinned rather than tracking `master` on purpose: an unrelated upstream commit
# should not turn every open Tickler pull request red. Bumping this is its own
# pull request, and a red CI on that bump is exactly the signal we want — it
# means a Paperclip upgrade broke Tickler, loudly, before a user hit it.
#
# One commit SHA, comments and blank lines ignored.

1b4c803816e82b0265c8422e1a804327a7ed8c54
